# text-processing: one line per script, for cheap discovery.
#
# Every script accepts -h/--help, reads a FILE argument or stdin, and writes
# to stdout, so they compose into pipelines. Options come before the file
# argument (llm-call.sh is the exception and accepts either order).
#
# Statistics scripts (ngrams, lexical-stats, tfidf, zipf, similarity,
# vocab-diff) take RAW TEXT and tokenize internally.
# Filters (stopwords, dedup) take ONE TOKEN OR RECORD PER LINE and compose
# with tokenize.sh.
#
# Limits: the word-level scripts (tokenize --words, ngrams, lexical-stats,
# tfidf, zipf, similarity, vocab-diff) are ASCII-only, and the chunkers are
# for prose and Markdown, not source code. See docs/text-processing.md.

## 1. Corpus hygiene
pii-redact.sh          Mask emails, keys, IPs, cards and PEM blocks; --check exits 1 on findings.
normalize-text.sh      Fold smart quotes, strip control chars, rejoin words split across lines.
strip-markup.sh        Reduce HTML or Markdown to the prose inside it.

## 2. Tokenization and sizing
tokenize.sh            Emit one word, sentence, paragraph or character per line; --count for frequencies.
token-estimate.sh      Estimate tokens (chars/4) and cost; --budget N exits 1 when over.

## 3. Vocabulary statistics
stopwords.sh           Drop stopwords from a token stream (whole-line literal match).
ngrams.sh              Count word n-grams via the paste-shift trick; -n 2 for bigrams.
lexical-stats.sh       Tokens, types, type/token ratio, hapax, sentence length.
tfidf.sh               Document frequency, idf and per-document tf-idf over a corpus.
kwic.sh                Keyword in context: every hit with surrounding words.
zipf.sh                Compare observed word frequencies with Zipf's prediction.

## 4. Chunking for retrieval
chunk-text.sh          Sentence-aligned chunks with configurable size and overlap.
chunk-markdown.sh      One chunk per section, labelled with its heading path.

## 5. Deduplication and similarity
dedup.sh               Remove duplicate lines, order-preserving or sorted.
similarity.sh          Jaccard and containment between two documents; --shingles for near-duplicates.
vocab-diff.sh          Terms added and removed between two documents.

## 6. LLM input and output
extract-codeblocks.sh  Pull fenced code blocks out of Markdown or model output.
to-jsonl.sh            Turn text into JSONL records, escaped with jq.
jsonl-stats.sh         Validity and length report for a JSONL dataset.
prompt-template.sh     Fill ${PLACEHOLDER} slots; missing values are an error, no eval.
diff-outputs.sh        Word-level diff of two model outputs; exits 1 when they differ.

## 7. Calling a model
llm-call.sh            Call the Claude Messages API; key from the environment only.
llm-batch.sh           Run llm-call.sh over many files, resumable, with a manifest.

## Demo
pipeline-demo.sh       Walk a document through the whole collection. No API key needed.
